# Docker-level environment for the devcontainer, loaded via the
# --env-file runArg in devcontainer.json.
#
# sync-common.sh copies this template to devcontainer.env on the host before the
# build if that file is absent. Docker fails hard when --env-file points at a
# missing file, and devcontainer.env is gitignored, so without that bootstrap a
# fresh clone could not start the container at all.
#
# Most configuration now lives in site.env, which common/setup.sh sources
# directly and which IS committed. Use this file only for values that must be
# present in the container environment before setup.sh runs - for example a
# corporate proxy. It is gitignored, so it may hold machine-specific values.

# HTTP_PROXY=
# HTTPS_PROXY=
# NO_PROXY=
